From 992d6dce7f83025e2766bbff20171f573d9e2550 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Grasso <me@leonardograsso.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 01:03:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(mermaid-text): join sequence lifelines to messages

Lifelines were dashed (U+2506), which terminals draw with gaps, and a message replaced the source lifeline cell and put its arrowhead on the target's, so nothing joined. Lifelines are now solid; a message starts from a junction on a bare lifeline, crosses other lifelines with a cross, and keeps the target lifeline with the arrowhead beside it. Activation bar edges, notes and self-messages keep their drawing.
---
